RESIZE REGRESSION  ratio=1.1145, recorded 0.8650 +/-10%. A configure now costs 1.11 times what the same restyle, relayout and repaint costs when a content change asks for it, over the same four documents in this same run. A configure is doing work the document change is not: look for work proportional to the document being done more than once per configure.
Both slopes are in the line above: the one that moved is the one to look at. Resize is out of the compositor programme's scope, so this is a gate against regressing it by accident — if the change was deliberate, move `RECORDED` in `crates/zgui-bench/src/bin/resize-slope/verdict.rs` in a commit that changes nothing else and says why.
